Added Apple Speech and Foundation Models services, concrete PocketTTSService and PhononTTSService providers sharing AppleNativeTTSService in the Apple namespace, an in-process transport, RTVI delivery, and AppleVADAnalyzer for SoundAnalysis confidence scores. The host's per-session provider selection drives a standard ServiceSwitcher, and native playback validates each request's provider tag. Native audio remains outside Python while standard context aggregators and turn strategies handle speech boundaries, interruptions, and played-text history. User turns require a recognized word alongside native acoustic activity, so noise-only VAD spikes cannot interrupt replies; ordered ASR finalization preserves short and resumed utterances.

Foundation Models preparation hints now use committed played-text context after responses and interruptions. Shared history retains bounded whole turns for native token-budget selection, while the host prewarms single-use sessions without reusing generated-but-unplayed text.
